Dear Vang,

There is still a misunderstanding.  You can do the analysis just as easily 
using either voom-limma or edgeR, but you cannot combine the two.  You 
certainly cannot input voom output to edgeR.

You simply use:

dge <- calcNormFactors(dge)
dge <- estimateGLMCommonDisp(dge, design)
dge <- estimateGLMTrendedDisp(dge, design)
dge <- estimateGLMTagwiseDisp(dge, design)
fit <- glmFit(y, design)
lrt <- glmLRT(fit, contrasts=c(3,5))
topTags(lrt)

Once the design matrix is made, it's just the same basic pipeline as for 
any example in the edgeR User's Guide.

Best wishes
Gordon


