Not exactly.

While the LRT is a test of significance for differences of any level of the
factor, I would not expect it to be exactly equal to the union of sets of
genes using Wald tests.

Use the LRT if you want to describe the set of genes from any level of
disease. Use the Wald tests if you want to describe the set of genes from
pairs of levels.

